                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I was very surprised with Sword Lord. I've tried two playthoughs so far and succeeded once. An average run takes about 20 minutes and the game saves the current wave you are on if you die, making it very accessible for players. It does lose your current run on exit though, so be aware.\n\nIt takes some blind learning to understand the mechanics of the swinging. Once you understand how to play, the different weapon types become very distinct and useful pending the style of play you want. Most revolve around weight and threat range, but that is okay since the Dev did the most important thing in the world for melee combat games; they made maces+warhammers hurt....A LOT. It was so satisfying one shotting mooks after winding up a swing.\n\nIt is short and doesn't have an endless wave mode, which really kills replay value. Still, for $1 and an enjoyable 1-2 hours of coin-op arcade like experience, it's really good. If it had local multiplayer and an Endless Mode, I could see this being very popular.\n\n6.5/10 due to low replay value.",
